-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",222,{
[7073]="70065B6E\n1\tTalk to King Elessar outside Iáphel\tKing Elessar has brought his soldiers to bear against the Corsair raiders that threaten Iáphel.\n2\tTalk to the Swan-knight Rossaran in Iáphel\tKing Elessar has asked you to go with the Swan-knight Rossaran to drive the Corsairs from northern Iáphel.\n3\tFind and defeat Corsairs hiding behind the northern buildings of Iáphel (total: 4)\tSearch for Corsairs hiding behind the northern buildings of Iáphel.\n4\tTalk to Rossaran among the northern buildings of Iáphel\tRossaran is waiting to hear your report among the northern buildings of Iáphel.\n5\tTalk to Gimli in the main square of Iáphel\tGimli remained in the main square of Iáphel to root Corsair raiders from out of hiding.\n6\tTalk to King Elessar by the shore\tYou and Gimli have caught up with King Elessar by the shore, down the hill from Iáphel.\n7\tKing Elessar has asked you to search along the shoreline for sign of Corsairs that did not take to their boats.\t\n8\tSearch along the shoreline for any sign of hidden Corsairs\tKing Elessar has asked you to search along the shoreline for sign of Corsairs that did not take to their boats.\n9\tSearch along the shoreline for any sign of hidden Corsairs\tKing Elessar has asked you to search along the shoreline for sign of Corsairs that did not take to their boats.\n10\tTalk to Orgolas outside his hiding-place\tWhat has brought Orgolas to this place? He was supposed to remain in Ost Arndír!\n11\tListen to Orgolas explain what befell Thorongil\tYou should listen to Orgolas's story.\n12\tTalk to Orgolas\tYou should listen to Orgolas's story.\n13\tTalk to King Elessar by the shore\tKing Elessar wears a thoughtful expression as he waits for you to speak to him.\n",
[7074]="7006D5AB\n1\tSpeak with Raphûz to begin the hunt for Urkhêru\tRaphûz prepares to enter the ruins where the great boar is said to stalk. Let him know when you are ready to proceed.\n2\tSpeak with Raphûz to continue the hunt for Urkhêru\tYou and Raphûz search the ruins for signs of Urkhêru but find nothing.\n3\tSpeak with Raphûz to continue the hunt for Urkhêru\tYou and Raphûz search the ruins for signs of Urkhêru but find nothing.\n4\tSpeak with Raphûz to continue the hunt for Urkhêru\tYou and Raphûz search the ruins for signs of Urkhêru but find nothing.\n5\tSpeak with Raphûz to engage Urkhêru\tAfter a short advance through the ruins, Raphûz stopped and spotted the beast, Urkhêru. He appears to be awaiting your signal to conclude the hunt.\n6\tSpeak with Raphûz\tYou found and killed Urkhêru. Raphûz looks pleased with your success. Speak with him.\n",
[7075]="7006C4B1\n1\tReady yourself for the Orcs\tThe Orcs have followed you to Enârshan's home. Defeat them and make safe the cave.\n2\tDefend against the attacking Orcs\tOrcs have arrived at Enârshan's home. Defeat them before they can cause any damage.\n3\tDefend against the attacking Orcs\tYou hear more Orcs coming. Defeat them before they can cause any damage.\n4\tDefend against the attacking Orcs\tThere are more Orcs on the way. Their captain appears to be with them. Defeat them before they can cause any damage.\n5\tSpeak with Enârshan\tYou do not hear any more Orcs. Enârshan's home is safe for now.\n",
[7076]="7004D3D5\n1\tTalk to Oroniel\tYou should talk to Oroniel.\n2\tHelp construct a barricade\tHelp construct a barricade.\n3\tDefend the workers from the spiders\tDefend the workers from the spiders.\n4\tHelp construct another barricade\tHelp construct another barricade.\n5\tDefend the workers from the spiders\tDefend the workers from the spiders.\n6\tHelp construct the final barricades.\t\n7\tDefeat the attacking spiders\tDefend the workers from the attacking spiders.\n8\tTalk to Thranduil\tTalk to Thranduil.\n",
[7077]="7000069D\n1\tTalk to Radagast\tYou have travelled with Radagast into the corrupted swamp of Agamaur. Aid him as he travels to the Eglain-encampment to the west.\n2\tTalk to Dannasen\tThe leader of the shades resides at the seemingly abandoned Eglain-encampment. The defeat of Dour-root has opened the way into the western ruins, where the shades Radagast spoke of dwell. Radagast asked that you entreat with Dannasen, their leader, for their aid.\n3\tDefeat Neven\tNeven's throne is further northward into the ruins. Neven holds some sway over the shade-captain, Dannasen. Perhaps if you speak with him you may find a way to alter Dannasen's orders.\n4\tSpeak to Dannasen\tDannasen lingers at the Eglain-encampment to the south of Neven's throne. Neven, the shades' commander, was actually a wight summoned by Ivar to contain the shades. With his destruction, Dannasen may now be willing to aid you.\n5\tFollow Radagast deeper into Agamaur\tFollow Radagast as he moves deeper into Agamaur. Dannasen, renewed, called forth his men to battle and opened the way westward. It may be that now you will be able to reach Elsa and Eriac.\n6\tTalk to Elsa the Bold\tSpeak to Elsa to learn more about her battles in Agamaur. Thanks to Dannasen and his men, the way westward into Agamaur was opened, and you were able to reach Elsa and Eriac.\n7\tSpeak to Radagast\tThe gate into Garth Agarwen lies to the north. Elsa has sent you to seek Ivar at Garth Agarwen and put an end to him.\n8\tSpeak to Radagast\tSpeak to Radagast to see if there is something else he would have you do. Radagast has driven the Gaunt-lord Ivar from Agamaur and stopped his nefarious plans...for now.\n",
[7078]="70034C1B\n1\tSpeak with Edsig\tEdsig and Gárferth are prepared to defend the city of Forlaw, or die trying. They are encouraged by Thrymm's arrival, knowing that he could probably single-handedly defeat the attacking Orcs.\n2\tDefeat the Orcs assaulting Forlaw (total: 54)\tThe Orcs have arrived with a rather large raiding party. This attacking force is quite possibly the largest to ever march on the city of Forlaw.\n3\tPush back the final assault\tThe Orcs marching on Forlaw are almost defeated, but the worst is yet to come. They are spurred on by two lumbering and brutal war-trolls.\n4\tReturn to Edsig\tThe enemy attack has been broken, and Forlaw remains unscathed. However, that this many Orcs are marching on the roads of Wildermore is troubling.\n",
[7079]="7000B8AB\n1\tTalk to Calenglad\tCalenglad is on the slope by Barad Rath. The Dúnedain have come to Barad Rath to remember their fallen, and Calenglad is waiting to walk with you to the site.\n2\tTake your place next to Cuguminuial\tThe Dúnedain have come to Barad Rath to mourn the loss of their kin.\n3\tWatch the building of the cairn\tThe Dúnedain have come to Barad Rath to mourn the loss of their kin.\n4\tPlace cap-stone on the cairn for Carchammadel\tThe Dúnedain are waiting for you to place the cap-stone on the cairn for Carchammadel.\n5\tWatch the building of the cairn\tThe Dúnedain have come to Barad Rath to mourn the loss of their kin.\n6\tPlace cap-stone on the cairn for Colhamnir\tThe Dúnedain are waiting for you to place the cap-stone on the cairn for Colhamnir.\n7\tWatch the building of the cairn\tThe Dúnedain have come to Barad Rath to mourn the loss of their kin.\n8\tPlace cap-stone on the cairn for Tadan\tThe Dúnedain are waiting for you to place the cap-stone on the cairn for Tadan.\n9\tListen to Calenglad\tThe Dúnedain have come to Barad Rath to mourn the loss of their kin.\n10\tTalk to Calenglad\tFleet-wing brings a dreaded, but expected, message: Amarthiel's troops have begun passing through the Evendim Gate in search of Narchuil.\n",
[7080]="70003281\n1\tFind Avorthal\tAvorthal is being held on the \"Irestone,\" the ship docked at the port-city of Kheledûl. Unless you free him tonight, the \"Irestone\" will carry Avorthal far from rescue and doom Ered Luin to war between dwarves and Elves.\n2\tTalk to Avorthal\tAvorthal is on the deck of the \"Irestone,\" still docked at Kheledûl. The Captain of the \"Irestone\" has been defeated. You should speak with Avorthal and make your escape.\n",
[7081]="7006C6FA\n1\tJoin Raphûz and Ashâmi\tRaphûz and Ashâmi are sitting and talking. You should sit and join them.\n2\tAshâmi and Raphûz asked you to sit with them.\t\n3\tListen to the conversation between Ashâmi and Raphûz\tYou sat with your friend and the woman, Ashâmi. They seem to be talking more openly, learning about one another.\n4\tRespectfully leave the conversation by bowing to either Raphûz or Ashâmi\tAs Raphûz and Ashâmi converse, you saw a figure approach. You should investigate.\n5\tSpeak to the new arrival\tYou saw a shadow approach. You should investigate.\n",
[7082]="7000070B\n1\tSpeak with Candaith\tYou have arrived at the foot of Weathertop to discover that Orcs from the South have made their way to the crest. Candaith awaits your assistance in driving the war-band from the ruins of Amon Sûl.\n2\tSpeak with Candaith\tA small force of goblins greeted you at the foot of Weathertop. Candaith has sent you upon the path to the left, while he will clear the path to the right, meeting once again upon the crest of Weathertop.\n3\tDefeat Bûb-hosh\030Defeat Muz\tCandaith sent you up one branch of the path up Weathertop, while he took the other, in search of the leaders of the Orc war-band.\n4\tSpeak with Candaith at Weathertop's peak\tSomewhere above you on the path, Candaith waits to speak with you again. You have defeated two of the leaders of the Orc war-band.\n5\tDefeat Rigûl\030Defeat Rigûl's minions\tYou have found the leader of Saruman's expedition, the Uruk Rigûl. You must defeat Rigûl and his minions to break their will and drive them from the Weather Hills.\n6\tSpeak with Candaith\tThe Uruk-hai expedition lies in ruins. You have won the day. You should speak with Candaith.\n",
[7083]="7001BA27\n1\tTalk to Candaith\tYou have arrived at the foot of Weathertop to discover that Orcs from the South have made their way to the crest. Candaith awaits your assistance in driving the war-band from the ruins of Amon Sûl.\n2\tTalk to Candaith\tA small force of goblins greeted you at the foot of Weathertop. Candaith has sent you upon the path to the left, while he will clear the path to the right, meeting once again upon the crest of Weathertop.\n3\tDefeat Bûb-hosh\030Defeat Muz, the Warg-keeper\tCandaith sent you up one branch of the path up Weathertop, while he took the other, in search of the leaders of the Orc war-band.\n4\tTalk to Candaith at Weathertop's peak\tSomewhere above you on the path, Candaith waits to speak with you again. You have defeated two of the leaders of the Orc war-band.\n5\tDefeat Rigûl\030Defeat Rigûl's minions\tYou have found the leader of Saruman's expedition, the Uruk Rigûl. You must defeat Rigûl and his minions to break their will and drive them from the Weather Hills.\n6\tTalk to Candaith\tThe Uruk-hai expedition lies in ruins. You have won the day. You should speak with Candaith.\n",
[7084]="7006B70E\n1\tTalk to Corudan inside Ashâgir\tCorudan needs your help if he is to reach the chamber deep within Ashâgir where the last stockpile of Hungry Fire was hidden. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tTalk to Rothog inside Ashâgir\tDeep within Ashâgir, Rothog is ready to do his part.\n",
[7085]="7001AC1B\n1\tTalk to Magor\tIn the depths of Azanarukâr, Magor wishes to fight alongside you in search of the artifact he believes Gorothúl left there.\n2\tDestroy Gorothúl's beacon\tYou have found the relic within Azanarukâr, and should destroy it to prevent further of Gorothúl's schemes from hatching.\n3\tDefeat Gwathnor\tGwathnor has awakened, and he must be defeated in order to prevent the growth of his power. Do not allow Gwathnor or any of his minions to approach the door. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n4\tTalk to Magor\tMagor is waiting to speak with you in the depths of Azanarukâr after your defeat of Gwathnor and the forms of Grawulun.\n",
[7086]="70072137\n1\tTalk to Sorkamâl\tYou have arrived in the royal living quarters. You should talk to Sorkamâl.\n2\tCollect historical tomes (total: 10)\tSorkamâl fears valuable tomes may be destroyed in the fighting in Emax Dûl. You should collect historical tomes in the royal living quarters.\n3\tTalk to Sorkamâl\tYou have collected as many tomes as you can carry. You should talk to Sorkamâl.\n4\tInvestigate the Sai's bed-chamber\tSorkamâl would like to check one more location before you leave. You should investigate the Sai's bed-chamber.\n5\tInvestigate the artifact piece\tYou have found a strange broken statue near the Sai's bed. You should investigate the artifact piece.\n6\tSorkamâl is curious to learn more about the broken artifact. You should collect the remaining artifact pieces.\t\n7\tAssemble the artifact\tYou have collected the pieces of the artifact. You should assemble the artifact by placing the pieces on the bottom section.\n8\tDefeat Dúrkhamos the Far-reaching\tAn Ordâkhai sorcerer has appeared and threatens you! You should defeat Dúrkhamos the Far-reaching.\n9\tDestroy the Thardúth statue\tThe statue you assembled exudes a fell aura. You should destroy the assembled Thardúth statue.\n",
[7087]="70052CCE\n1\tTalk to Skalla\tThe Great Goblin's forces are approaching. You should talk to Skalla.\n2\tWitness the battle\tThe Great Goblin's forces are approaching, and will soon clash with those of the hobgoblin warlord.\n3\tWitness the battle\tBattle has been joined!\n4\tTalk to Langhár\tThe battle has been won! You should talk to Langhár.\n",
[7088]="7002980A\n1\tTalk to Edhere\tSpeak with Edhere and tell him to lead his men out of the mine.\n2\tTalk to Ondor\tSpeak with Ondor and release him from his cell.\n3\tTalk to Meriun\tSpeak with Meriun and tell him to lead his men out of the mine.\n4\tTalk to Ondor\tFight your way towards the forges and free any slaves you come across.\n5\tTalk to Ondor\tFight your way up onto the platforms to reach the bridge spanning the cavern.\n6\tTalk to Ondor\tThe shortest way out of the Orc-mines lies across a long trestlebridge that spans the cavern. It is likely to be the most perilous step of your escape.\n7\tTalk to Ondor\tYou must make your way up the slopes, then fight your way past any remaining Orcs to the exit of the caverns.\n",
[7089]="700375C5\n1\tTalk to Reeve Fríthild\tYou should speak with Reeve Fríthild.\n2\tDefeat the Warg-riders\tDefeat the Warg-riders terrorizing the eastern fields of the Broadacres.\n3\tTalk to Reeve Fríthild\tYou should speak with Reeve Fríthild.\n",
[7090]="70027E9C\n1\tHear Guto's proposition\tGuto is at his encampment. You should speak with Guto.\n2\tFollow Guto\tGuto is at his encampment. You should speak with Guto.\n3\tNotify Elder Riagán that Guto brings a guest\tThe Elder is in Lhan Tarren. You should notify Elder Riagán that Guto is arriving soon with the half-orc guest from Isengard.\n4\tMake sure that the servant of Isengard keeps to his peaceful intentions\tGuto and the servant of Isengard are just behind you. You should observe the meeting with the Elder and make sure that nothing goes awry.\n5\tTalk to Elder Riagán\tThe Elder looks like he wishes to speak with you. You should talk to Elder Riagán.\n",
[7091]="70028388\n1\tTalk to Lhucu\tTalk to Lhucu.\n2\tClear the path of wights\tClear a path through the wights for Lhucu.\n3\tTalk to Lhucu\tLet Lhucu know that the path has been cleared below.\n4\tDefeat Trehéarn Brenin\tConfront and defeat Trehéarn Brenin.\n5\tDefeat Mostun\tBanish the fell spirit Mostun from the mortal world.\n6\tTalk to Lhucu\tSpeak with Lhucu.\n7\tWithdraw through the main gate\tLeave Lhan Gogledh as the Huntsman commanded.\n",
[7092]="700214A0\n1\tPlace the amulet on Cadelhin's tomb\tSeek out the tomb of Cadelhin within the barrow and place the amulet thereon.\n2\tListen to Cadelhin's tale\tListen to Cadelhin's tale.\n3\tTalk to Cadelhin\tProtect Cadelhin from the shades that seek to do him harm.\n",
[7093]="70026FC9\n1\tTalk to the Rohirrim herald\tDefend the herald of the Rohirrim from his ambushers.\n2\tBlow the Horn of the Rohirrim\tOverwhelming numbers of wild men are approaching. Summon the Rohirrim to your aid.\n3\tDefeat the Dunlending attackers\tHold out until reinforcements arrive.\n4\tWith the battle over, the herald you strove to protect lies dying. You speak to him, hoping to bring his final words to his allies at the Ford of Isen.\t\n",
[7094]="700598BF\n1\tTalk to Marigold\tMarigold is waiting for you to catch up before venturing further into the Old Forest.\n2\tDefend Marigold\tYou should defend Marigold as she guides you through the forest.\n3\tTalk to Marigold\tMarigold has found the tree-creatures. You should talk to her and come up with a plan.\n4\tEavesdrop on the tree-creatures\tMarigold has suggested eavesdropping on the tree-creatures. If one of the creatures leaves, it may be possible to stop the remaining two together.\n5\tDefend Marigold\tMarigold has challenged the tree-creatures.\n6\tTalk to Marigold\tThe tree-creatures have been defeated.\n",
[7095]="7006B06F\n1\tTalk to Rothog the Storm\tRothog has summoned you to his chambers to confront Zarzíra Dawn-star about her misdeeds.\n2\tDefeat Zarzíra and her men\tDefeat Zarzíra and her men as they attack you in the audience chamber.\n3\tSpeak to Rothog\tSpeak to Rothog the Storm about Zarzíra's treachery.\n",
[7096]="70028FAC\n1\tDiscover the source of the Dunlending supplies\tDiscover the source of the Dunlending supplies.\n2\tDefeat Orcs in the cavern (total: 7)\tDefeat the Orcs that inhabit the cavern beneath Cuvnerth.\n",
[7097]="7005A80A\n1\tTalk to Gori\tGori waits for you by the side of the River Kibil-nâla.\n2\tTalk to Gori on the bridge\tGori continues his way through the ruins, too distracted to notice any imminent danger.\n3\tTalk to Gori by the plaque\tGori has paused to speak with you before the next set of stairs.\n4\tTalk to Gori\tGori is catching his breath after the battle and motions you over to talk with him.\n",
[7098]="70035837\n1\tSearch the roadway for sign of Byre Tor refugees\tThe Orc roadway stretches through much of Balewood. Sensing that the refugees may be nearby, you decide to search the barren roadway for any sign of Byre Tor refugees before more Orcs return.\n2\tDefeat the refugee's attackers (total: 2)\tThe man's attackers can be found on the roadway. You have discovered a man of Byre Tor fleeing from vicious wood-trolls of Balewood.\n3\tTalk to Húna\tHúna can be found along the Orc roadway in Balewood. Having saved the man from certain doom, you should now speak to him to learn of his plight and the fates of the other refugees.\n4\tFollow Húna deeper into Balewood\tHúna is travelling along the Orc roadway in Balewood. You should aid Húna in seeking out his fellows in Balewood.\n5\tTalk to Húna\tHúna is on the roadway in Balewood. The snarls of Orcs in the distance have cut short Húna's heroics, and you should speak to him to discern what action is to be taken.\n6\tFollow Húna deeper into Balewood\tHúna is running north-east of the roadway in Balewood. Húna believes that his fellows might be found off the side of the road in Balewood. You should continue to follow and protect him.\n7\tFollow Húna and Bebbe to the Orc roadway\tThe Orc roadway can be found to the west of the cave Húna discovered. Húna has reunited with Bebbe, but during their conversation the frantic screams of one of their fellows nearby has filled them with grave concern.\n8\tApproach the Uruk captain, Voskor\tThe Uruk captain can be found along the roadway in Balewood. Húna's fellow, Leodwald, has been wounded and captured by a vile Uruk captain of Isengard. You should confront the Uruk before any more harm can come to the Rohirrim.\n9\tDefeat the attacking Orcs (total: 2)\tThe Orc attackers can be found on the roadway in Balewood. In response to your defiance, the Uruk captain has set his Orcs upon you. They must be defeated if the refugees are to escape the forest alive.\n10\tTalk to Leodwald and confront Voskor\tLeodwald can be found laying on the roadway in Balewood. You should speak to Leodwald about his condition before confronting the Uruk captain a second time.\n11\tAttempt to stand against Voskor and his force\tYou are frozen in fear as the ground trembles - you must wait to see what unfolds.\n12\tFlee to the cave with the Byre Tor refugees\tThe cave can be found to the east of the Orc roadway. The Uruk captain has been brutally defeated by a raging Huorn. You should flee for safety while the Huorn pursues the wounded Uruk into the woods.\n13\tTalk to Húna and flee into the cave\tHúna can be found outside the cave to the east of the roadway in Balewood. You have escaped certain defeat from a powerful Uruk captain and a vicious Huorn, and should now seek shelter with the other refugees in the nearby cave.\n",
[7099]="700571DE\n1\tApproach the gathering in the woods\tApproach the gathering in the woods.\n2\tLet events transpire\tLet events transpire.\n3\tTalk to Runerik\tTalk to Runerik.\n4\tRun wild!\030Roar to the wilds!\tRun wild!\n",
[7100]="7006EB80\n1\tMove closer to speak with Numûru and Razâl\tMove closer to speak with Numûru and Razâl.\n2\tListen to Numûru and Razâl's conversation\tListen to Numûru and Razâl's conversation.\n3\tSpeak with Numûru\tSpeak with Numûru outside Kûr Anzar.\n4\tSpeak with Razâl\tSpeak with Razâl outside Kûr Anzar.\n5\tMove further into Kûr Anzar\tMove further into Kûr Anzar.\n6\tMove further into Kûr Anzar\tMove further into Kûr Anzar.\n7\tCollect grain sacks (total: 8)\030Destroy racks of weapons (total: 6)\030Defeat Barkhûshim sentries (total: 9)\tSabotage the Barkhûshim forces in Kûr Anzar by taking grain sacks, destroying weapon stands and defeating Barkhûshim sentries.\n8\tMeet Numûru and Razâl outside the tower of Kûr Anzar\tMove to meet Numûru and Razâl outside the Angar Aragín, the tower of Kûr Anzar at the top of the city.\n9\tSet fire to the barricades near the tower\tSet fire to the barricades near the tower.\n10\tListen to Numûru\tListen to Numûru near Angar Aragín.\n11\tSpeak with Razâl\tSpeak with Razâl near Angar Aragín, the tower of Kûr Anzar.\n",
[7101]="700576CB\n1\tTalk to the Emissary\tYou should talk to the Emissary in the Mountains of Shadow Chamber.\n2\tSpeak the Words\tThe Emissary has asked you to speak the pass code in \"the King's chosen language\". You should speak the words to the Emissary.\n3\tTalk to the Emissary\t\n4\tUnlock the door\tYou have the key! You should unlock the door and retrieve the second stone!\n5\tTake the second stone\tThe door is open! You should retrieve the second stone!\n",
[7102]="7004E920\n1\tTalk to Náth\tNáth can be found at the Bitter Scar. You have travelled to the end of the Bitter Scar with Dori and Company, you now prepare to search for the remains of Vethúg Wintermind. You should speak to Náth.\n2\tFind Dori, Glóin, and Bofur in the Bitter Scar\tDori, Bofur, and Glóin have ventured into the Bitter Scar. You should follow Dori, Bofur, and Glóin into the Bitter Scar.\n3\tTalk to Dori in the Bitter Scar\tDori can be found in the Bitter Scar. You have travelled to the end of the Bitter Scar and rejoined Dori and Company, but there is no sign of the remains of Vethúg Wintermind.\n4\tSigns of battle can be found at the end of the Bitter Scar. You have come upon the aftermath of a struggle between Vethúg Wintermind and an unknown foe. You should examine the signs of battle to determine what has happened.\t\n5\tDeliver the black arrow to Dori\tDori can be found in the Bitter Scar. You have discovered that a great struggle occurred between Karazgar and Vethúg Wintermind, and it seems Karazgar was the victor. You should speak to Dori at once.\n6\tLeave the Bitter Scar with Dori and Company\tDori can be found in the Bitter Scar. You have discovered concerning evidence that Karazgar may have slain or taken Vethúg Wintermind from the Bitter Scar. You should leave at once with Dori and Company.\n7\tWitness the meeting of the companies of Dori and Ingór\tIngór, son of Vékun, has come to the Bitter Scar with a company of his own and appears eager to speak to Dori and Company. You should remain on guard and defend Dori and Company if the need arises.\n8\tTalk to Dori\tDori can be found in the Bitter Scar. Ingór has revealed himself to be a Prince of the Zhélruka, and he has offered Dori and Company safe passage to Skarháld. You should speak to Dori and see if he wishes to accept.\n",
[7103]="70057E6A\n1\tTalk to Léothred\tTalk to Léothred.\n2\tListen to Léothred's tale\tListen to Léothred's tale. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[7104]="7004D3CF\n1\tExamine Scatha's tooth\tExamine Scatha's tooth with Fróthi.\n2\tExperience the vision\tExperience the vision.\n3\tTalk to Fróthi\tTalk to Fróthi.\n",
})
